    "tiny.columns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc94e11b5c867827",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "## 2. Read an error and find the problem\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine that we tried to select a column named `seat` and Python showed this message:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "KeyError: 'seat'\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Start with the **last line**. `KeyError: 'seat'` means Python could not find the label `seat`. Save that label so we can check it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "614cab4b6cef8021",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "wrong_column = \"seat\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f46a82ed875fd40b",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Ask whether that label is in the table’s column names. Predict `True` or `False` before running it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6ec681305cddb713",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "wrong_column in tiny.columns"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7b84948fa84cfd7",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Compare the requested label with the available names. The table has `seats`, with an **s**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b26ce54a944b75e5",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "correct_column = \"seats\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "59a39f9201a8920d",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Select the repaired column and save it as `seat_counts`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "04fa47cbc78ce45b",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seat_counts = tiny[correct_column]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7aa6f212d77b4712",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Show the values in the repaired column."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "86e755edd69c4dd4",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seat_counts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d564bad75208c26",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "## 3. Notice the missing value\n",
    "\n",
    "`NaN` means a value is missing. It does not mean zero. Ask which place has a missing seat count."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4adcd3f44623330a",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seat_counts.isna()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5680dad7f2b52fcb",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Count how many seat values are missing. In Python, `True` counts as 1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "85c5eb708909d8d3",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seat_counts.isna().sum()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e66daceb7d30bad1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Keep only the seat counts that are present."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "28f691712fcd1dff",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "observed_seats = seat_counts.dropna()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "96cd2f814211f0bd",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Show the observed values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "75b75e3e3bb9e963",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "observed_seats"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1628b3489251bf38",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Find the average of the observed seat counts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b9214efa45bf4e8a",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "observed_average = observed_seats.mean()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6ca9086332344eef",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Show the observed-value average."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a4573c7114ca31c3",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "observed_average"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "12fefa1c4e50722e",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "## 4. Compare a different missing-value choice\n",
    "\n",
    "Here we temporarily replace the missing seat count with zero. This asks a different question because an unknown count becomes a known zero."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "39710864f66b3972",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "zero_filled_seats = seat_counts.fillna(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "910f18efe500597b",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Show the values after filling the missing value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6c0d03225e8fd914",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "zero_filled_seats"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4cccb41f342cc3f5",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Find the average after replacing the missing value with zero."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "23b49c488db25e6c",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "zero_filled_average = zero_filled_seats.mean()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bd2539c5928d24c3",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Show the new average. Is it the same as the observed-value average?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1ca30a365ea6a5eb",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "zero_filled_average"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "345629659092bf55",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "## 5. Choose rows after the repair\n",
    "\n",
    "First, remove rows where the seat count is missing. This gives us a table with observed seat counts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "25078144f892d9da",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "known_seats = tiny.dropna(subset=[\"seats\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7074e31244cc9868",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Make a rule that asks which observed counts are at least 20."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9b2b2edd80e6e016",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "has_20_seats = known_seats[\"seats\"] >= 20"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "814492cab52ea54d",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Use the rule to keep those rows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "92b3bfcd3c247e96",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "larger_places = known_seats[has_20_seats]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ded7fff8d6587f9b",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Show the result."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c4dca025f492aa1f",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "larger_places"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8ee5b01b44c5b998",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "## 6. Make and use a function\n",
    "\n",
    "A function gives a short name to a reusable action. `count` is the input. The `return` line sends a result back."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f3015a1da9f98234",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "function-definition"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def seat_message(count):\n",
    "    return f\"{count} seats available\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "21414d74819b0416",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Call the function with the number 18. The value inside the parentheses becomes `count`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1c430fd2a6463f75",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seat_message(18)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b3252888e94b3299",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "Call the same function with our observed-value average."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7aecc3467898a470",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "seat_message(observed_average)"
   ]
  },
